From 3850a79ea1e407fbd2faf5a009a99501bafde4d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:52:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 47/58] serve: /v1/load counts what really waits and takes a
 sustained rate as its 100 %

The first /v1/load reported "free 15, idle, run now" while an image request had the engine alone, counted
requests waiting for the control lines twice and missed those waiting for a slot. It now reads the admission
state in one place (StrataEngine.load_counts: slots taken, waiting, admitting, standing back behind an image
request, the image line) and reports would_wait / image_alone. The 100 % mark is the token count over 10 s while
half the slots or more decode (a one-second figure could be a burst and the peak only rises); the peak file is
written atomically with the config it was measured with (STRATA_LOAD_PEAK_FILE moves it), bad values are not
taken, and GET /load also answers vLLM's server_load figure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
